---
description: Protect README, docs, examples, and changelog from collateral rewrites
globs: README.md,docs/**/*.md,examples/**/*.py,CHANGELOG.md,AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md
alwaysApply: false
---

# Docs and examples

- Prefer additive or surgical edits over full-file rewrites.
- When updating for a release, add or refresh sections; do not delete positioning, roadmap, architecture, or contributor/build material unless superseded and replaced.
- Examples should show the observation API (`ObservationInput`, tenant-scoped `recall`).
- Keep CHANGELOG in Keep a Changelog format with Added/Changed/Fixed as appropriate.
- `CLAUDE.md` must remain a thin pointer to `AGENTS.md`.
- If aligning docs to a PRD, still follow shipped code and existing repo structure.
